  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129114,
      "id": "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799",
      "title": "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1c13bce0-76ea-57d2-aa71-29a6a4fd98ed",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{23}=5$ is in the same column as the leading entry $a_{13}=1$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e3ca8d26-29d5-57a3-ab6c-a3b40f16aea2",
          ":answer-field/key": "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$",
