  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129114,
      "id": "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799",
      "title": "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dafefbc1-0e73-5750-af9c-37d88f6b21db",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "80b2656e-aca5-5801-a962-5c49cafc7034",
