      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the fourth row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -8 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form.",
